TITLE:: InsightLoudness
summary:: loudness the way ITU-R BS.1770 and EBU R128 mean it
categories:: Libraries>Insight
related:: Classes/Insight, Classes/InsightSpectrum

DESCRIPTION::
The loudness half of link::Classes/Insight::, on its own. The server does the part that has to run per sample - the K-weighting filter and a running mean square over the last 100 ms - and hands one block of those mean squares, one per channel, to this ten times a second. Everything else is bookkeeping, worked out here in the language.

code::
l = InsightLoudness(2);
l.add([0.001, 0.001]);         // one block: mean square per channel
l.momentary;                   // -> LUFS, the last 400 ms
l.shortTerm;                   // -> LUFS, the last 3 s
l.integrated;                  // -> LUFS, everything since reset, gated
l.range;                       // -> LU, the loudness range
l.maxMomentary; l.maxShortTerm;
l.reset;
::

The four measures follow BS.1770 and EBU R128 / Tech 3342:

list::
## strong::momentary:: - the mean of the last four blocks (400 ms).
## strong::shortTerm:: - the last thirty blocks (3 s).
## strong::integrated:: - every block since reset, gated: blocks below -70 LUFS are dropped, then blocks more than 10 LU below the mean of what is left are dropped too, and the rest is averaged.
## strong::range:: (LRA) - the spread between the 10th and 95th percentile of the short term values, after a -70 LUFS absolute and a -20 LU relative gate.
::

The gated statistics are histograms 0.1 LU wide, so a session that has run for hours costs no more per block than one that has run for seconds. Silence is answered as code::-inf::. A 5.1 layout weights the surrounds by +1.5 dB and leaves the LFE out; any other channel count is weighted evenly.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
ARGUMENT:: channels
how many channels a block carries.
RETURNS:: an InsightLoudness.

METHOD:: loudnessOf
The loudness of a weighted mean-square power, in LUFS: code::-0.691 + 10 * power.log10::, or code::-inf:: for silence.

METHOD:: weightsFor
The channel weights for a layout: code::[1, 1, 1, 0, 1.41, 1.41]:: for 5.1 (six channels), even otherwise.

METHOD:: absoluteGate
METHOD:: relativeGate
METHOD:: rangeGate
The gate thresholds, in LU: -70 absolute, -10 relative for the integrated value, -20 relative for the range.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

private:: prMean, prWeighted, prBin, prBinLoudness, prIntegrated, prRange

METHOD:: add
One block: the mean square of the K-weighted signal, one value per channel. Updates every measure.
ARGUMENT:: powers
an Array of mean-square values, one per channel.
RETURNS:: this.

METHOD:: momentary
METHOD:: shortTerm
METHOD:: integrated
METHOD:: range
The four measures, in LUFS (LU for range).

METHOD:: maxMomentary
METHOD:: maxShortTerm
The highest momentary and short term values since reset.

METHOD:: duration
Seconds integrated: the blocks are 100 ms each.

METHOD:: channels
How many channels a block carries.

METHOD:: reset
Forget everything: the histograms, the ring of recent blocks, the held maxima.

EXAMPLES::

code::
// a constant -20 dBFS block, K gain taken out, reads -20.7 LUFS
l = InsightLoudness(2);
40.do { l.add([0.005, 0.005]) };
l.integrated;                  // ~ -20.69
l.reset;
::
